# Pure generated/derived output only -- never useful for diagnosing a bug, and often large.
# gitignore syntax; no negation support; VS Code Copilot reads this at extension startup only
# (restart the window after editing).
#
# Same philosophy as the five sibling repos' .copilotignore files: exclude Category 1 (build
# output nobody debugs from) and keep Category 2 (config, lockfiles, properties) visible, since
# config is where this project's real bugs have actually lived -- the pydantic-settings
# CORS-parsing crash found in Step 0 is this repo's own example already.
#
# ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM THAT PRECEDENT: .env is excluded here, unlike every sibling repo.
# Those repos' .env files hold only local, non-sensitive demo credentials (a throwaway Postgres
# password). This repo's .env holds a REAL OpenAI API key once configured -- an actual secret, not
# a hypothetical one -- so it is excluded on that basis alone. .env.example (no real values) stays
# visible, same as everywhere else.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage
coverage/
htmlcov/

# Corpus build artifacts -- Markdown is the source (stays visible); these are generated from it.
# See corpus/README.md.
corpus/pdf/
corpus/figures/

# The one real secret in this repo -- see the note above.
.env

